        UNFALSIFIED is not a bug report; it is the absence of one. It says only that
        nothing in the always-on lane has ever watched this instrument disagree, so a
        broken one and a working one would look the same. Guard D lived here for its
        whole life while the Rust screen's question ('has it got a caller?') said WIRED.
      
        READ THE UNFALSIFIED COUNT HERE AS A PROPERTY OF THIS SCREEN, NOT AS A VERDICT ON
        bench/'s TESTS. Polarity is detected from `pytest.raises`, and most bench
        instruments are TOTAL functions: they return a token (`STEADY`, `MARGINAL_TAIL`,
        `NO_STEADY_TAIL`, `SOLE_TENANT`) instead of raising, so a test that watches
        `gpu_steady_tail` refuse a series is invisible to the raise-based model. This is the
        same limit already recorded for `classify_` in the harness domain. `unfalsified`
        here means THIS SCREEN has not seen a disagreement, which is exactly what R12 says
        it should say, and not that no test watches one. Crediting a polarity this screen
        did not observe would be the Guard D shape with the sign flipped.
        Handed to Niobe: a value-polarity model for total instruments, or a note per row.
      
